import{_ as t,o,c as r,a2 as s}from"./chunks/framework.BM5YPQmL.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Internals: entropy and the crypto core","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"internals/drbg-crypto.md","filePath":"internals/drbg-crypto.md"}'),a={name:"internals/drbg-crypto.md"};function d(i,e,c,n,h,l){return o(),r("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[s(`<h1 id="internals-entropy-and-the-crypto-core" tabindex="-1">Internals: entropy and the crypto core <a class="header-anchor" href="#internals-entropy-and-the-crypto-core" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Internals: entropy and the crypto core&quot;">​</a></h1><p>The RNG and the primitive families the protocols (TLS, SSH, the OTA verifier) build on. Implementation: <code>ocos/services/crypto/</code> - <code>interface/svc_crypto_{api,core,aead,bn, curve25519,ec_nist,rsa,sha512,x509}.h</code> and matching <code>src/</code> modules, plus <code>src/svc_crypto_irq_window.h</code>, <code>src/svc_crypto_roots.h</code> (generated), <code>src/svc_crypto_dh_scale_vectors.h</code>. Usage: <code>cryptotest</code> / <code>dhtest</code> (the L1 face IS the test face).</p><h2 id="_1-the-drbg-sp-800-90a-hmac-drbg" tabindex="-1">1. The DRBG (SP 800-90A HMAC_DRBG) <a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-the-drbg-sp-800-90a-hmac-drbg" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;1. The DRBG (SP 800-90A HMAC_DRBG)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Header comment (verbatim intent): &quot;BUG-0106 (A4-02) replaced the old timer-seeded xorshift32 with an HMAC_DRBG (SP 800-90A): RDRAND-seeded when the CPU offers it, RDTSC + boot-jitter re-mixed otherwise, instantiated at first use and reseeded on demand. The DRBG state is protected by the crypto IRQ window (BUG-0294, A4-07) so concurrent kthreads can never observe the same generated block.&quot;</p><p>Implementation facts:</p><ul><li>State: <code>static u8 drbg_k[32]; static u8 drbg_v[32]; static int drbg_ready;</code></li><li><code>drbg_update</code> implements NIST SP 800-90A section 10.1.2: <code>K = HMAC(K, V || 0x00 || data); V = HMAC(K,V); if data: K = HMAC(K, V||0x01||data); V = HMAC(K,V)</code></li><li>Entropy gather <code>drbg_entropy32</code>: RDRAND (CPUID-checked, <code>rdrand %0 ; setc %1</code>) 8 bytes at a time; the fallback mixes <code>rdtsc_now()</code> and weak sources; the final xor with <code>rdtsc ^ (core_timer_ticks() &lt;&lt; 1)</code> lands on bytes 24-31.</li><li><strong>Why it matters</strong> (the old xorshift32 was catastrophically weak): &quot;past and future key the kernel ever generated is computable by a passive observer. Both the SSH server and the TLS client were effectively transparent.&quot;</li><li>The RDRAND wrapper&#39;s <code>setc</code> flag is the u8/&quot;=q&quot; inline-asm constraint the stricter CI assembler forced into correctness - see <a href="./../dev/portability.html">../dev/portability.md</a>.</li><li>The <strong>IRQ window</strong> (<code>svc_crypto_irq_window.h</code>): a single-core save/cli/restore pair (<code>pushfq; popq %0; cli</code> / <code>pushq %0; popfq</code>) used by the lazy initializers (AES inverse S-box, NIST curve tables) so concurrent kthreads never observe the same generated block or a half-built table. Host test builds expand it to nothing (documented as a build-environment property - &quot;NOT SMP protection and NOT a lock&quot;; the kernel is single-CPU).</li></ul><h2 id="_2-the-primitive-families" tabindex="-1">2. The primitive families <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-the-primitive-families" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2. The primitive families&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Family</th><th>Members</th><th>Validation</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Hash</td><td>SHA-256 (one-shot + streaming <code>crypto_sha256_ctx{u32 h[8]; u64 total; u8 buf[64]; int buflen;}</code>), SHA-384/512</td><td>NIST vectors via <code>cryptotest</code></td></tr><tr><td>MAC / KDF</td><td>HMAC-SHA-256 (RFC 2104), HKDF-Expand (RFC 5869), the TLS 1.3 key schedule (RFC 8446 section 7.1: <code>net_tls13_ks_expand_label</code> / <code>derive_secret</code>)</td><td>NIST vectors + RFC 8448 host tests</td></tr><tr><td>Symmetric</td><td>AES-128 block/CTR/CBC (FIPS-197), AEAD: AES-GCM, ChaCha20-Poly1305</td><td>RFC 8439 vectors, NIST GCM TC3/4 (host harnesses)</td></tr><tr><td>DH</td><td>big-int modexp: fixed 1024-bit (<code>DH_BYTES 128</code>, Oakley Group 1, RFC 2409) + generic <code>crypto_dh_modexp_n</code> (SSH group 14 2048-bit); embedded <code>crypto_dh_group1_prime/generator</code>, <code>crypto_dh_group14_prime[256]</code></td><td>python3 pow() goldens (the scale-sweep vectors)</td></tr><tr><td>RSA</td><td><code>svc_crypto_rsa.c</code> (verify paths for TLS/SSH; <code>RSA_DEBUG</code> is a source-local <code>#ifdef</code>)</td><td>openssl fixtures (SKIP-FIXTURE harness)</td></tr><tr><td>Elliptic</td><td>NIST P-256 ECDH/ECDSA (<code>ec_nist</code>), X25519 (<code>curve25519</code>)</td><td>RFC 7748 vectors, P-256 KAT (host harnesses)</td></tr><tr><td>Certificates</td><td>X.509 parse + CA chain validation + SAN dNSName hostname check (<code>x509</code>)</td><td>live-site chain fixtures (host harness)</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The numbered L1 extension set &quot;stays closed&quot; for encoding (Driver-API style extension); the crypto L1 surface is exactly 2 ops: <code>cryptotest</code> (op 1) and <code>dhtest</code> (op 2), both captured.</p><h2 id="_3-the-embedded-root-ca-store" tabindex="-1">3. The embedded root CA store <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-the-embedded-root-ca-store" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3. The embedded root CA store&quot;">​</a></h2><p><code>src/svc_crypto_roots.h</code>: &quot;Auto-generated by tools/embed_roots.py</p><ul><li>DO NOT EDIT BY HAND. Embedded root CA store (DER) for the X.509 chain validator.&quot; Raw DER byte arrays (an 809-line file) covering the public roots - e.g. <code>root_isrg_root_x1[]</code> (ISRG Root X1, 4096-bit RSA, valid 2015-06-04 -&gt; 2035-06-04), plus the ISRG X2, GlobalSign, GTS R1/R4, DigiCert, Baltimore, Amazon, Microsoft, Sectigo E46/R46 roots. The TLS client verifies server chains against this store; a self-signed chain is REFUSED by default (<code>config set tls.insecure 1</code> is the explicit opt-in - HTTPS E2E check 0).</li></ul><h2 id="_4-the-consumers" tabindex="-1">4. The consumers <a class="header-anchor" href="#_4-the-consumers" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;4. The consumers&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>TLS client</strong> (<code>services/net/src/svc_net_tls.c</code>): TLS 1.3 (X25519 + AES-128/256-GCM + ChaCha20-Poly1305, full HKDF key schedule, encrypted handshake, CertificateVerify) and TLS 1.2 (ECDHE_RSA AES-GCM 0xC02F/0xC030, ChaCha20 0xCCA8, legacy DHE AES-CBC 0x0067 fallback; TLS12 fallback retry with RFC 7507 SCSV). Transcript 32768 with overflow FLAGGED (BUG-0078); alert capture + truncation detection (BUG-0228).</li><li><strong>SSH client/server</strong>: KEX curve25519-sha256 (RFC 8731) preferred / diffie-hellman-group14-sha256 fallback; host keys rsa-sha2-256/512 + ssh-rsa; aes128-ctr preferred / aes128-cbc fallback; hmac-sha2-256. The host test server (<code>tools/paramiko_sshd.py</code>) logs the negotiated DH shared secret K for cross-checking against the kernel <code>dhtest</code>.</li><li><strong>OTA</strong>: the package SHA256 verifier.</li></ul><h2 id="_5-the-test-faces" tabindex="-1">5. The test faces <a class="header-anchor" href="#_5-the-test-faces" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;5. The test faces&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><code>cryptotest</code> (crypto op 1): header banner <code>&quot;Crypto self-test (NIST vectors):\\n&quot;</code> then per-primitive <code> SHA-256: PASS</code>-style lines (SHA-256, AES-128, HMAC-SHA256, HMAC-SHA384).</li><li><code>dhtest</code> (crypto op 2): DH modexp golden tests + ECDH/X25519 end-to-end checks (ok_e/ok_K PASS/FAIL lines) + <code>&quot;DH modexp scale sweep (truth vectors, python3 pow()):\\n&quot;</code>.</li><li>Host harnesses (<code>make test</code>): AEAD/SHA (RFC 8439 + NIST), bignum/P-256, X25519 (RFC 7748), RSA + X.509 (openssl fixtures, SKIP-FIXTURE declared), TLS 1.3 key schedule (RFC 8448 + KeyUpdate KATs), the P0 TLS batches (BUG-0022..0027, includes the kernel <code>net_tls.c</code> directly), the A401 negative-length DER probes at all four TLS entry points.</li></ul><h2 id="_6-audit-trail-notes" tabindex="-1">6. Audit-trail notes <a class="header-anchor" href="#_6-audit-trail-notes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;6. Audit-trail notes&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The famous crypto-adjacent fixes both regression-tested now: the TCP RX checksum chain bug (double complement) and the TLS mid-handshake hostname bug. The DRBG replacement (xorshift32 -&gt; HMAC_DRBG) is the load-bearing one: every key the kernel generates (SSH session keys, TLS premaster secrets) flows from <code>crypto_random*</code>.</p><h2 id="_7-the-l1-surface-2-ops-both-captured" tabindex="-1">7. The L1 surface (2 ops, both captured) <a class="header-anchor" href="#_7-the-l1-surface-2-ops-both-captured" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;7. The L1 surface (2 ops, both captured)&quot;">​</a></h2><div class="language-c vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">c</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">#define</span><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;"> L1SVC_CRYPTO_CRYPTOTEST</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> 1</span><span style="--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D;">   /* cryptotest              */</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">#define</span><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;"> L1SVC_CRYPTO_DHTEST</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">     2</span><span style="--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D;">   /* dhtest                  */</span></span></code></pre></div><ul><li><strong>Trigger</strong>: a developer or the regression gate runs <code>cryptotest</code> / <code>dhtest</code> at the ush prompt (or via <code>sysdiag</code>&#39;s selftest lab / the <code>run</code> mechanism).</li><li><strong>Processing</strong>: both route through <code>crypto_l1_dispatch</code> into <code>core_kcap_run_fn</code>-captured command bodies that iterate the vector tables and print PASS/FAIL per primitive.</li><li><strong>Impact</strong>: the PASS lines are regression anchors (check 11 of the 31-check gate); a FAIL here means the primitive tables or the DRBG changed behavior - stop shipping and diff first.</li></ul><p>Family declaration: <code>OC_SERVICE_DECL_L1(&quot;crypto&quot;, &quot;crypto service (aead/sha/rsa/dh/x509 + ring-3 surface)&quot;, 0, 0, crypto_l1_dispatch);</code></p><h2 id="_8-where-each-primitive-is-consumed" tabindex="-1">8. Where each primitive is consumed <a class="header-anchor" href="#_8-where-each-primitive-is-consumed" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;8. Where each primitive is consumed&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Primitive</th><th>Consumers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>HMAC_DRBG (<code>crypto_random*</code>)</td><td>SSH session keys, TLS premaster/traffic secrets, any nonce</td></tr><tr><td>AES-GCM / ChaCha20-Poly1305</td><td>TLS 1.3 record protection; TLS 1.2 GCM suites</td></tr><tr><td>AES-CBC</td><td>the legacy TLS 1.2 DHE-RSA-AES128-SHA256 (0x0067) fallback the HTTPS E2E pins</td></tr><tr><td>SHA-256/384/512 + HMAC</td><td>handshake transcripts, certificate digests, HKDF, the DRBG itself</td></tr><tr><td>HKDF / TLS 1.3 key schedule</td><td>RFC 8446 section 7.1 (<code>net_tls13_ks_expand_label</code>, <code>derive_secret</code>)</td></tr><tr><td>DH modexp (group 1 / group 14)</td><td>SSH KEX fallback (diffie-hellman-group14-sha256), the legacy TLS DHE suite</td></tr><tr><td>X25519 / P-256</td><td>TLS 1.3 + SSH curve25519-sha256 KEX; ECDH self-tests</td></tr><tr><td>RSA</td><td>TLS/SSH server-cert verification, ssh-rsa/rsa-sha2 host keys</td></tr><tr><td>X.509 + root store</td><td>the TLS client&#39;s chain validation + SAN dNSName hostname check</td></tr></tbody></table>`,24)])])}const m=t(a,[["render",d]]);export{u as __pageData,m as default};
